--- Retrieves info about one item in the current retrieved list of items from the Auction House.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `type`: One of the following:
--- - `index`: The index of the item in the list to retrieve info from (normally 1-50, inclusive)
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `name`: the name of the item
--- - `texture`: the fileID of the texture of the item
--- - `count`: the number of items in the auction item, zero if item is "sold" in the "owner" auctions
--- - `canUse`: true if the user can use the item, false if not
--- - `level`: the level required to use the item,
--- - `levelColHeader`: The preceding *level* return value changes depending on the value of levelColHeader:
--- - `minBid`: the starting bid price
--- - `minIncrement`: the minimum amount of item at which to put the next bid
--- - `buyoutPrice`: zero if no buy out, otherwise it contains the buyout price of the auction item
--- - `bidAmount`: the current highest bid, zero if no one has bid yet
--- - `highBidder`: returns name of highest bidder, nil otherwise
--- - `bidderFullName`: returns bidders full name if from virtual realm, nil otherwise
--- - `owner`: the player that is selling the item
--- - `ownerFullName`: returns owners full name if from virtual realm, nil otherwise
--- - `saleStatus`: 1 for sold 0 for unsold
--- - `itemId`: item id
--- - `hasAllInfo`: was everything returned
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetAuctionItemInfo)
declare function GetAuctionItemInfo(type: string, index: number): (string, number, number, number, boolean, number, string, number, number, number, number, string?, string?, string, string?, number, number, boolean)
