--- Retrieves information about a specific trade skill.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `skillIndex`: The id of the skill you want to query.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `skillName`: The name of the skill, e.g. "Copper Breastplate" or "Daggers", if the skillIndex references to a heading.
--- - `skillType`: "header", if the skillIndex references to a heading; "subheader", if the skillINdex references a subheader for things like the cooking specialties; or a string indicating the difficulty to craft the item ("trivial", "easy", "medium", "optimal", "difficult").
--- - `numAvailable`: The number of items the player can craft with his available trade goods.
--- - `isExpanded`: Returns if the header of the skillIndex is expanded in the crafting window or not
--- - `altVerb`: If not nil, a verb other than "Create" which describes the trade skill action (i.e., for Enchanting, this returns "Enchant"). If nil the expected verb is "Create."
--- - `numSkillUps`: The number of skill ups that the player can receive by crafting this item.
--- - `indentLevel`: 0 or 1, indicates whether this skill should be indented beneath its header. Used for specialty subheaders and their recipes.
--- - `showProgressBar`: indicates if a sub-progressbar must be displayed with the specialty current and max ranks. In the normal UI, those values are only shown when the mouse is over the sub-header.
--- - `currentRank`: is a the current rank for the specialty if showProgressBar is true.
--- - `maxRank`: is a the maximum rank for the specialty if showProgressBar is true.
--- - `startingRank`: is the starting rank where the specialty is available. It is used as the starting value of the progress bar.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetTradeSkillInfo)
declare function GetTradeSkillInfo(skillIndex: number): (string, string, number, boolean, string?, number, number, boolean, number, number, number)
