    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_EncounterTimeline.GetEventTimeRemaining)
    function GetEventTimeRemaining(eventID: EncounterTimelineEventID): DurationSeconds
    --- Returns a Duration object that tracks the elapsed duration of a timeline event. This object tracks the range [0, duration] of the event and automatically pauses its progression based on event state.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_EncounterTimeline.GetEventTimer)
    function GetEventTimer(eventID: EncounterTimelineEventID): LuaDurationObject?
    --- Returns information about the position of an event on the timeline.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_EncounterTimeline.GetEventTrack)
    function GetEventTrack(eventID: EncounterTimelineEventID): (EncounterTimelineTrack, number?)
    --- Returns a sorted list of event IDs present in the timeline from shortest to longest remaining durations, meeting the requirements of the specified filters.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `maxEventCount`: Maximum number of sorted events to return.
    --- - `maxEventDuration`: Maximum duration of sorted events to return.
    --- - `excludeTerminalStates`: If false, include events that are terminal states such as Canceled or Finished.
    --- - `excludeHiddenEvents`: If false, include events that should be hidden by user configuration, such as events on long tracks when the user has opted to not show long countdowns.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_EncounterTimeline.GetSortedEventList)
    function GetSortedEventList(maxEventCount: number?, maxEventDuration: DurationSeconds?, excludeTerminalStates: boolean?, excludeHiddenEvents: boolean?): EncounterTimelineEventID[]
